Jahshaka local patch 0021 (upstream-reportable): anisotropic voxel cone tracing
saturates its alpha against the cone's OWN starting surface, so the escape
fraction that weights the ambient term (`light.w` in computeVctProbe,
`light.xyz += ambient * light.w`) collapses at every anisotropic quality.

Mechanism: the per-axis textures are front-to-back composited along their axis
(AnisotropicMipVctStep1: a + b * (1 - a.a)), so a one-voxel-thick floor reads
as alpha 1.0 along +/-Y at every coarser mip regardless of how little of the
cell it fills. Correct for a ray crossing the cell; wrong for the diffuse cone
that starts ON that floor and re-enters its own cell as the footprint grows.
Measured (Jahshaka gi.ddgi_ambient, open floor, nothing above it, ambient only):
isotropic keeps 93% of the ambient, anisotropic kept 4%.

Fix: a second accumulator, `escapeAlpha`, that in the anisotropic loop takes the
MIN of the three axis composites one mip finer than the colour samples (the
axis textures are half-res, so lodLevel is already one mip coarser than the
isotropic march at the same distance) and that the ambient escape weight reads
instead of `alpha`. Colour/alpha accumulation (the bounce) is untouched; the
isotropic path computes the identical expression, so isotropic pixels are
byte-for-byte unchanged. In the cascaded path the next cascade's escapeAlpha
starts from the previous cascade's colour alpha (signature unchanged) -- a small
approximation only that path pays.

Measured (open floor, % of the raw ambient): shipped anisotropic 4.3%; min3 at
lodLevel 26.1%; min3 at lodLevel - 1 (this patch) 65.2%; the main texture's own
isotropic mip alpha (exact, available when vct_enable_specular_sdf_quality) 94.6%
-- REJECTED because it also restores the isotropic path's leak through one-voxel
walls: sealed sample rooms went +46/+51 of 255 at Medium and clipped, where this
patch moves them +7 (the isotropic march's own leak on those rooms is +14).

MEDIA-ONLY (Samples/Media/Hlms/Pbs/Any/Vct_piece_ps.any): no Ogre rebuild, but
every tree must run the patch loop -- Studio stages Hlms media from the source
tree. Verified: `git apply --check` against the pristine pin, `--reverse --check`
after applying. Rationale also in irisgl/docs/OGRE_BUILD.md, entry 21.

